    Solves the tree to star transformation problem.

    The key insight is that we can always transform any tree to a star graph.
    The minimum number of operations equals max_degree - 2, where max_degree
    is the maximum degree of any vertex in the original tree.

    This is because:
    - A star has one center with degree n-1 and all other nodes have degree 1
    - Each operation can increase/decrease degrees strategically
    - The formula (max_degree - 2) gives the minimum operations needed
    """
    # Parse input
